Z||000000||FieroJoe||06-16-2001||10:52 PM||||With my new white face gauges (overlays), they look really cool at night with the orange lighting, but the needles are hard to see because they blend in so well to the color.  I like the look of them during daytime, but I was wondering, what options do I have for nighttime?  What colors are found in other cars that would look just as good during the day as they would at night?<P>I have ruled out repainting the inside of the instrument panel, as all the other "dash light color changing" topics I have read have had bad results with these.<P>Oh, almost forgot, 85mph cluster non backlit gauges.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||06-17-2001||12:08 PM||||I painted mine silver, but that probablt wouldn't help your cause much. <BR>Just take the dash apart again, lightly sand the needles (I didnt even take mine out) and paint em say...  darker red or something. =)||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||06-17-2001||12:20 PM||||Hi, i just did my guages with the white overlay, looks great, i painted my needle bright red(i have an Indy fiero, so the white gauges with red interior and red gauge needles looks pretty good!!), looks good at night too, alot better than the original black gauges..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||4
